  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe growth-ring planner (`adaptive/grow.rs`) was bounded only by #13's length budget (revolution length in tool radii). Its time goes into whole-ring polygon work on every trial step, and that work per tool radius depends on the shape. On the island fixture it ran ~53 s (release, this machine; the issue measured ~68 s) before the length budget refused it.\n\nA third budget law in `adaptive/budget.rs` (`Work`, `GEOM_MAX`) now counts the **polygon vertices each trial step works through**: the cleared area it offsets, the ring it opens, and each revolution's margin area. The count is summed over every margin attempt, like the length budget. Past **500,000** vertices the plan is refused by name:\n\n> adaptive: the HSM plan is refused: growing the cleared area ran past its planning budget after 88 revolutions - its rings (~502 k outline vertices worked, over 500 k) are too detailed to plan in seconds (an island?); a trochoid ... - Offset rings cut this pocket instead\n\n- **Deterministic, no wall clock.** The same project plans, or is refused, on every machine and under any load. No wall-clock backstop was added: the vertex bound already caps the time.\n- **Fallback unchanged.** The refusal uses the existing `refused` path, so `pocket_hsm`'s named trochoid -> Offset-ring fallback is the same and the island's fallback output is identical (162 moves, same report line).\n- **Length budgets unchanged.** `LEAST_WORK_MAX` and `WORK_MAX` did not need to move.\n- `mod.rs` stays at 435 lines: the `Cell<f64>` field became `budget::Work`.\n- Counters use saturating arithmetic. No unwrap, expect or panic outside tests.\n\n**Why vertices.** Trial count does not separate the cases: the island and the slot both spend ~550 trials. The up-front estimate does not either: the island reads 339 r and the slot 113 r, both far under 2,000. Time follows vertex count to within ~2x. Full reasoning and the dropped options are in `docs/decisions/850-adaptive-geometry-budget.md`.\n\n## Calibration (deterministic counts, measured with a local probe that is not committed)\n\n| fixture (suite) | ends | vertices | share of 500 k |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 60 x 14 slot (`adaptive_hsm` pocket) | Done | 252,328 | 0.50 |\n| 60 x 14 slot (`adaptive::tests` plan) | Done | 246,290 | 0.49 |\n| 60 x 22 channel (`adaptive_hsm`) | Done (then trochoid/rings, unchanged) | 175,217 | 0.35 |\n| whole_model_pocket, largest corner | Done | 73,496 | 0.15 |\n| motion level_links | Done | 37,545 | 0.08 |\n| pocket_overhead / machining2d | Done | 34,508 | 0.07 |\n| 14 / 20 mm band, shoulder_adaptive | refused up front (#13) | 0 | - |\n| island 60 x 40, 12 x 12 | **refused** after 88 revs | 502,660 | > 1 |\n\nBefore this change the island spent 865 k vertices in its first margin attempt, and 1.95 M in its second before the length budget refused it. Margin: every fixture that grows today stays at least **1.98x** under the budget, pinned at 1.9x.\n\n## Bound in seconds (this machine, the whole island pocket: growth, trochoid refusal, Offset rings)\n\n| | before | after |\n|---|---|---|\n| island, release | 52.6 s | **19.0 s** |\n| island, debug | not measured (well over a minute by the same ratio) | **38.7 s** |\n| 14 mm band, release | 0.14 s (refused up front) | same |\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n1. `adaptive_hsm::the_island_is_refused_by_the_geometry_budget_in_seconds` (default lane, ~39 s debug). Checks:\n   - the refusal is named;\n   - the vertex count in the note lies in 500..=520 k, so it was refused within one revolution of the budget (deterministic);\n   - the Offset rings cut the pocket, chained and finite;\n   - **the verifier is silent** on them (solid law included);\n   - a loose wall-clock backstop: 600 s debug, 60 s release.\n2. `adaptive::tests::a_channel_is_grown_as_one_spiral_that_never_crosses` (existing debug test) now also asserts that the slot's plan spends at most 1/1.9 of the budget.\n3. `adaptive::budget::fixtures::the_fixtures_that_grow_today_stay_under_the_geometry_budget`: the slot and channel pockets, 1.9x margin. It runs ~140 s in debug, so it is `#[ignore]`d into the heavy lane (release `--ignored`).\n4. `adaptive::budget::tests::the_geometry_budget_refuses_by_name_and_saturates`: the `Work` unit test (refusal names, saturation, and that NaN length is ignored).\n\n## Gate\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: **green** (motion lib + adaptive_band + adaptive_hsm + pocket3d_hsm, 103 s).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- With the budget compiled in, these debug suites all passed:\n  - motion: lib, adaptive_band, adaptive_hsm, level_links, machining2d, machining3d, pocket3d_hsm, rotary_adaptive, rotary_dflat;\n  - app: pick_agnostic, pocket_overhead, pocket3d_hsm, probe_op, project_roundtrip, roughing2d, shoulder_adaptive, stock_engine_agreement, whole_model_pocket, level_links.\n- Release: the new island pin and `hsm_one` (island) were run; the island's fallback report line is unchanged.\n\n**Goldens.** No committed `.cl`/`.nc` golden is an adaptive pocket. Every plan that finished before still finishes with the same count path. The length check is evaluated first, so a plan refused by length keeps its old message. The code path only adds a counter and a check at each revolution start.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- **Heavy lanes that run Adaptive, not run (per the brief):**\n  - `rotary_adaptive` (three ignored tests on the developed bar);\n  - motion `pocket3d_hsm::the_stepped_block_...`;\n  - app `pocket3d_hsm::the_users_bore_...`;\n  - `adaptive_hsm::hsm_report_full_resolution`.\n\n  Their growth counts are unmeasured. If one of them now reads \"too detailed\" where it planned before, that is a regression to report: please run those lanes in the review or at the cut. This is the main residual risk.\n- The new heavy-lane margin test itself was not run with `--ignored` (its two pockets' counts are the measured 252 k / 175 k above, taken from the same code).\n- The debug \"before\" time for the island.\n\n## What this means for #845\n\n#845's held fix (`issue/7-r10-corner-reading`) roughly doubles growth work.\n- **Island:** it would now be refused at the same 500 k vertices, in the same ~19 s, instead of running even longer. The bound holds.\n- **Slot:** it spends 252 k today, so a doubling would put it at or over the budget. #845 must re-measure the slot and channel counts. If they cross 500 k, it raises `GEOM_MAX` with numbers (the pin in `budget_fixtures.rs` and `adaptive::tests` will tell it), rather than refusing the slot.\n\nEffort: high (no escalation).\n\nChangelog: Adaptive: the growth planner is now also bounded by the polygon geometry it works through (deterministic), so an islanded area it cannot finish is refused by name in seconds (island fixture ~19 s instead of ~1 min) before the named Offset-ring fallback\n\nFixes #850\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
